      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A crystallization method was proposed to assess disturbances in the lipid system; it was based on the interaction of a serum lipid fraction with a lecithin matrix. A total of 255 invidividuals were examined. A model experiment was performed by using chemically pure cholesterol (96 samples) and 10 different cholesterol esters (240 samples). There were a great differences in the frequency of various pattern structural types (homogeneous texture, fan crystals) in the healthy persons and patients. The test results were found to be related to the ratio of esterified to non-esterified cholesterol in the serum lipid fraction. The application of rheopolyglucin, , hemosorption, quantum hemotherapy in the patients contributed to normalization of crystallization test indices."},
